  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Common consumables have a reserve supply and a small reorder allowance; a restock card can show remaining quantities and outstanding orders.\", \"decision\": \"How should shared consumables be replenished?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe steward counts shared consumables at the end of each opening day and updates the restock card before ordering. A regular inventory combines several small shortages into one considered replenishment decision.\nMembers mark the restock card when a consumable reaches its minimum line, and the steward orders a replacement. Replenishment starts when actual use crosses a visible threshold rather than waiting for a full inspection.\nA rotating member checks shared consumables at each week’s first session and gives the steward a completed restock card. Responsibility for noticing shortages is shared while purchasing remains with the same accountable person."
    }
  ],
